# Kaggle Notebook environment — copy to .env.kaggle in your project root.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# STEP 1 — Upload HDF5 data as a Kaggle Dataset
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Your HDF5 files are in Drive at:
#   MyDrive/Thesis_Final/fake-news-data-for-thesis/processed_data/hdf5/
#     ├── coolant_train.h5   (~2.7 GB)
#     ├── coolant_dev.h5     (~0.35 GB)
#     └── coolant_test.h5    (~0.83 GB)
#
# Upload them to Kaggle keeping the folder structure:
#   a) Go to kaggle.com → Datasets → New Dataset
#   b) Name it, e.g. "fake-news-hdf5-data" → slug becomes "fake-news-hdf5-data"
#   c) Upload the three files inside a folder called "processed_data/hdf5/"
#      so the dataset layout is:
#        processed_data/hdf5/coolant_train.h5
#        processed_data/hdf5/coolant_dev.h5
#        processed_data/hdf5/coolant_test.h5
#   d) In your notebook → Add Data → search for your dataset
#      Kaggle mounts it at: /kaggle/input/fake-news-hdf5-data/
#
# Update DATA_ROOT below to match the slug you chose in step (b).

DATA_ROOT=/kaggle/input/fake-news-hdf5-data

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# STEP 2 — Make the project source code available on Kaggle
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Option A — Clone from GitHub (add this cell ABOVE cell 0 in the notebook):
#   !git clone https://github.com/<you>/fake-news-detection.git /kaggle/working/fake-news-detection
#   (No env var needed — the default KAGGLE_PROJECT_ROOT already uses this path)
#
# Option B — Upload project as a Kaggle Dataset:
#   Zip the project (exclude *.h5 and .git/), upload, add as input
#   Then set a Kaggle Secret: KAGGLE_PROJECT_ROOT=/kaggle/input/<your-code-slug>

# Platform identifier (used by env_utils.py)
PLATFORM=kaggle

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOTE: Checkpoints and MLflow logs are automatically redirected to
# /kaggle/working/ (writable) — no manual changes needed in the notebook.
# Download them from the Kaggle notebook output panel after the run.
